<p>
  A <a href="https://github.com/basecamp/lexxy">Lexxy</a> editor synced through
  <a href="https://github.com/jpcamara/lexxy-realtime">lexxy-realtime</a>.
  Lexical stores the document as nested <code>Y.XmlText</code> nodes. Each room
  has a <code>Note</code> record, which <code>NoteChannel</code> creates when
  the first person joins. The page gives your browser a signed token for this
  room and the note's <code>body</code> field, and the channel rejects any
  token that wasn't issued for that field.
</p>
<p>
  After each update, the server renders the full document to HTML with
  <code>Y::Lexxy</code> and writes it to <code>body</code>, a plain text
  column. yrby's tests compare that renderer's output byte for byte with HTML
  captured from a live Lexxy editor. The panel below fetches the column over
  HTTP, so you can watch the stored HTML change as you type.
</p>
